@*
    The right column: one item, read by its kind, and the acts on it.

    The four decisions — Move to backlog, Move to list, Defer, Archive — sit in
    a bar fixed at the foot of the column, each naming its key, so a long
    article never scrolls them out of reach. Only the item's body scrolls; the
    bar stays. Once an item has been routed or archived the decisions go except
    "Move to list", filing being allowed in every state.

    The header is the library's SectionHeader with the two acts that are not
    the decision the item is waiting for in its Actions slot: have a plan
    drafted about it, or delete it. "Create plan" stays when it cannot run,
    disabled with its reason on the title, because unavailability never hides
    an act; "Delete" removes an item whatever became of it.

    What the body shows depends on the kind. A video gets its thumbnail and the
    link; an article or a link gets the link and whatever excerpt was captured;
    an email its sender, subject and body; code a code block; an image the
    picture; a document its attachment; everything else its text as markdown.
    Today's captures mostly carry a title and nothing more, so the empty-body
    line is written to read well rather than as an error — it is the ordinary
    case, not a broken one.

    Beneath the suggestions sits Related: the other items that look like the
    same capture — choosing one opens it — and the tasks that already carry this
    one, each with the reason in words. The Inbox never acts on a relation; the
    two acts that do — "Archive as duplicate of…" and "Link to task…" — live
    here rather than in the header, which is at its budget, and are offered only
    while the item is open. Each opens a picker: a Modal with a SearchBox over a
    MenuList, the related ones first. An item archived as a duplicate says which
    item it duplicates on its state line.

    Above the pickers sit the suggestions: the tags, repositories and destination
    Classification proposes, each a numbered row the reader takes with the digit
    drawn on it, with Enter, or with a click, and turns down with its ×. Nothing is
    applied until then, and a chip turned down is recorded by the module and
    not offered for this item again. The digits are read here and on the list —
    wherever the reader's focus is while deciding. The article takes focus
    (tabindex -1, out of the tab order) so a click on its text is enough to put
    the keys here. Never from a field: the
    pickers stop the key on its way up, so typing "2" into the tag picker adds a
    "2" rather than taking the second chip.

    The pickers write through the state, and the state reloads: a tag or a
    repository is a decision the module records, not something this component
    holds. Repositories come from the settings store — the same list the Tasks
    pane and the Repositories screen read — so what is chosen here is something
    the backlog can actually target. Tags come from both sides of the join: the
    inbox's own items and, through the state's port, the words the backlog
    already files entries under — so a tag used there is a pick here rather
    than a retype.
*@

<div class="inbox-pane__column inbox-pane__column--detail" data-testid="inbox-pane-column-detail">
    @if (State.SelectedItem is not { } item)
    {
        <EmptyState Title="Choose an item"
                    Description="What it is, where it came from and what you can do with it appear here."
                    BaseClass="empty-state inbox-pane__empty-state"
                    TestId="inbox-detail-empty" />
    }
    else
    {
        var open = item.Status is InboxStatus.Unprocessed or InboxStatus.Deferred;
        var repos = item.RepoIds.Count;

        @* Only the article scrolls; the decisions bar below it stays put. *@
        <article class="inbox-pane__detail"
                 aria-labelledby="inbox-detail-title"
                 data-inbox-kind="@item.KindSlug"
                 data-testid="inbox-detail"
                 tabindex="-1"
                 @onkeydown="OnShortcutKeyAsync">
            <SectionHeader BaseClass="inbox-pane__detail-header"
                           TextCssClass="inbox-pane__detail-text"
                           EyebrowCssClass="inbox-pane__detail-eyebrow"
                           TitleCssClass="inbox-pane__detail-title"
                           ActionsCssClass="inbox-pane__detail-actions"
                           Level="3"
                           TitleId="inbox-detail-title"
                           Eyebrow="@Eyebrow(item)"
                           Title="@Title(item)"
                           TestId="inbox-detail-header">
                <Actions>
                    <ButtonGroup AriaLabel="Item actions" CssClass="inbox-pane__action-row" TestId="inbox-detail-action-row">
                        @if (open)
                        {
                            <AppButton Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                       Variant="ButtonVariant.Ghost"
                                       Disabled="@(!Availability.Available || State.RouteRunning || State.BulkRunning)"
                                       Busy="@State.PlanRunning"
                                       BusyLabel="Drafting a plan"
                                       Title="@(Availability.Available ? "Ask the AI for an import plan and add it to the backlog" : Availability.Reason)"
                                       OnClick="State.CreatePlanAsync"
                                       TestId="inbox-create-plan">Create plan</AppButton>
                        }
                        <DeleteButton Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                      Disabled="@Busy"
                                      OnClick="() => _deleteOpen = true"
                                      TestId="inbox-delete" />
                    </ButtonGroup>
                </Actions>
            </SectionHeader>

            @if (!open || item.Status == InboxStatus.Deferred)
            {
                <Alert BaseClass="inbox-pane__state"
                       Role="status"
                       Message="@StateLine(item)"
                       TestId="inbox-detail-state" />
            }

            <div class="inbox-pane__content" data-testid="@($"inbox-detail-kind-{item.KindSlug}")">
                @Thumbnails(item)

                @switch (item.Kind)
                {
                    case ContentKind.YouTube:
                        @if (YouTubeVideoId(item.SourceUrl) is { } videoId)
                        {
                            <a class="inbox-pane__media" href="@item.SourceUrl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-testid="inbox-detail-thumbnail-link">
                                <img class="inbox-pane__thumbnail"
                                     src="@($"https://img.youtube.com/vi/{videoId}/hqdefault.jpg")"
                                     alt="@($"Video thumbnail: {Title(item)}")"
                                     loading="lazy"
                                     data-testid="inbox-detail-thumbnail" />
                            </a>
                        }
                        @Link(item.SourceUrl)
                        @Prose(item, "Only the title and the link were captured.")
                        break;

                    case ContentKind.Article:
                    case ContentKind.Link:
                        @Link(item.SourceUrl)
                        @Prose(item, "Only the title and the link were captured; open it to read.")
                        break;

                    case ContentKind.Email:
                        <dl class="inbox-pane__facts">
                            <dt>From</dt>
                            <dd data-testid="inbox-detail-sender">
                                @if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(item.Person))
                                {
                                    <span>Unknown sender</span>
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    <TagChip Text="@TagText.Display(item.Person)" CssClass="inbox-pane__person" />
                                }
                            </dd>
                            <dt>Subject</dt>
                            <dd data-testid="inbox-detail-subject">@Title(item)</dd>
                        </dl>
                        @Prose(item, "The message body was not captured.")
                        break;

                    case ContentKind.ClaudeArtifact:
                        @Link(item.SourceUrl)
                        @Prose(item, "No summary was captured with the artifact.")
                        break;

                    case ContentKind.Code:
                        @if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(item.BodyMd))
                        {
                            @Note("No code was captured with the title.")
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <CodeView Source="@item.BodyMd"
                                      Language="@CodeLanguage(item.BodyMd)"
                                      AriaLabel="Captured code"
                                      CssClass="inbox-pane__code"
                                      TestId="inbox-detail-code" />
                        }
                        @Link(item.SourceUrl)
                        break;

                    case ContentKind.Image:
                        @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(item.SourceUrl))
                        {
                            <a class="inbox-pane__media" href="@item.SourceUrl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-testid="inbox-detail-image-link">
                                <img class="inbox-pane__image" src="@item.SourceUrl" alt="@Title(item)" loading="lazy" data-testid="inbox-detail-image" />
                            </a>
                        }
                        @Attachment(item.SourceUrl)
                        @Prose(item, null)
                        break;

                    case ContentKind.Document:
                        @Attachment(item.SourceUrl)
                        @Prose(item, "Only the title and the attachment were captured.")
                        break;

                    case ContentKind.Voice:
                        @Prose(item, "No transcript was captured with the memo.")
                        @Link(item.SourceUrl)
                        break;

                    default:
                        @Prose(item, "Only the title was captured.")
                        @Link(item.SourceUrl)
                        break;
                }

                @FileRows(item)
            </div>

            @if (open && State.Suggestions.Count > 0)
            {
                @* Numbered rows, the digit first: the number is how a reader who
                   has just read the item takes one without reaching for the
                   mouse. A suggestion no key takes — one that cannot be taken
                   yet — has no number and no button, and says why. *@
                <section class="inbox-pane__suggestions" aria-labelledby="inbox-detail-suggestions-title" data-testid="inbox-detail-suggestions">
                    <div class="inbox-pane__suggestions-head">
                        <h4 class="inbox-pane__suggestions-title" id="inbox-detail-suggestions-title">Suggested next step</h4>
                        <span class="inbox-pane__hint">press the number to take it</span>
                    </div>
                    <ol class="inbox-pane__suggestion-list">
                        @foreach (var suggestion in State.Suggestions)
                        {
                            var chip = suggestion;
                            var shortcut = State.ShortcutFor(chip);
                            <li class="inbox-pane__suggestion"
                                @key="chip.Key"
                                title="@SuggestionLabel(chip)"
                                data-suggestion-key="@chip.Key"
                                data-testid="@($"inbox-suggestion-{SuggestionTestId(chip)}")">
                                @if (chip.Available)
                                {
                                    <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.None"
                                               BaseClass="inbox-pane__suggestion-take"
                                               Disabled="@Busy"
                                               aria-label="@SuggestionLabel(chip)"
                                               aria-keyshortcuts="@shortcut"
                                               OnClick="() => State.AcceptSuggestionAsync(chip)">
                                        @if (shortcut is not null)
                                        {
                                            <kbd class="inbox-pane__key inbox-pane__suggestion-key" aria-hidden="true">@shortcut</kbd>
                                        }
                                        <span class="inbox-pane__suggestion-text">@SuggestionText(chip)</span>
                                        <span class="inbox-pane__suggestion-reason">@chip.Reason</span>
                                    </AppButton>
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    <span class="inbox-pane__suggestion-take inbox-pane__suggestion-take--unavailable">
                                        <span class="inbox-pane__suggestion-text">@SuggestionText(chip)</span>
                                        <span class="inbox-pane__suggestion-reason">@chip.UnavailableReason</span>
                                    </span>
                                }
                                <IconButton AriaLabel="@($"Dismiss {SuggestionText(chip)}")"
                                            Title="@($"Dismiss {SuggestionText(chip)}")"
                                            BaseClass="btn btn--ghost btn--icon inbox-pane__suggestion-dismiss"
                                            OnClick="() => State.DismissSuggestionAsync(chip)">×</IconButton>
                            </li>
                        }
                    </ol>
                </section>
            }

            @if (State.RelationsOf(item) is { } relations && (open || relations.Items.Count > 0 || relations.Tasks.Count > 0))
            {
                <section class="inbox-pane__related" aria-labelledby="inbox-detail-related-title" data-testid="inbox-detail-related">
                    <h4 class="inbox-pane__suggestions-title" id="inbox-detail-related-title">Related</h4>
                    @if (relations.Items.Count == 0 && relations.Tasks.Count == 0)
                    {
                        <Alert BaseClass="inbox-pane__note"
                               Role="status"
                               Message="Nothing else in the Inbox or the backlog looks like this item."
                               TestId="inbox-related-none" />
                    }
                    @if (relations.Items.Count > 0)
                    {
                        <ul class="inbox-pane__related-list" aria-label="Related items" data-testid="inbox-related-items">
                            @foreach (var relation in relations.Items)
                            {
                                var other = relation;
                                <li class="inbox-pane__related-row" @key="other.Id" data-relation="@other.Kind" data-testid="@($"inbox-related-item-{other.Id:N}")">
                                    <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.Ghost"
                                               Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                               Title="Open this item"
                                               CssClass="inbox-pane__related-open"
                                               OnClick="() => State.SelectItem(other.Id)"
                                               TestId="@($"inbox-related-open-{other.Id:N}")">@TitleOf(other.Title)</AppButton>
                                    <span class="inbox-pane__related-reason">@other.Reason · @InboxLabels.Status(other.Status)</span>
                                </li>
                            }
                        </ul>
                    }
                    @if (relations.Tasks.Count > 0)
                    {
                        <ul class="inbox-pane__related-list" aria-label="Related tasks" data-testid="inbox-related-tasks">
                            @foreach (var relation in relations.Tasks)
                            {
                                var task = relation;
                                <li class="inbox-pane__related-row" @key="task.Id" data-relation="@task.Kind" data-testid="@($"inbox-related-task-{task.Id:N}")">
                                    <span class="inbox-pane__related-title">@TitleOf(task.Title)</span>
                                    <Badge Kind="status"
                                           Slug="@(task.IsOpen ? "ready" : "done")"
                                           CssClass="inbox-pane__related-badge">@(task.IsOpen ? "Open" : "Done")</Badge>
                                    <span class="inbox-pane__related-reason">@task.Reason</span>
                                </li>
                            }
                        </ul>
                    }
                    @if (open)
                    {
                        <ButtonGroup AriaLabel="Relation actions" CssClass="inbox-pane__related-actions" TestId="inbox-related-actions">
                            <AppButton Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                       Disabled="@Busy"
                                       Title="Archive this item as the same capture as another one"
                                       OnClick="OpenDuplicatePicker"
                                       TestId="inbox-archive-duplicate">Archive as duplicate of…</AppButton>
                            <AppButton Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                       Disabled="@Busy"
                                       Title="Record that a task already in the backlog is this item, without making a new one"
                                       OnClick="OpenLinkPicker"
                                       TestId="inbox-link-task">Link to task…</AppButton>
                        </ButtonGroup>
                    }
                </section>
            }

            @* Keys typed into a picker are the picker's: stopping them here ends
               Blazor's walk up to the article, whose digits take a suggestion. *@
            <div class="inbox-pane__pickers" @onkeydown:stopPropagation="true">
                @if (open)
                {
                    <TagMultiSelect Label="Tags"
                                    Id="@TagsInputId"
                                    Options="@State.TagOptions"
                                    SelectedValues="@TagNames(item)"
                                    SelectedValuesChanged="tags => State.SetTagsAsync(tags)"
                                    AllowCreate="true"
                                    Placeholder="Add a tag"
                                    CssClass="inbox-pane__picker"
                                    TestId="inbox-detail-tags" />
                    <TagMultiSelect Label="Repositories"
                                    Options="@State.RepositoryOptions"
                                    SelectedValues="@item.RepoIds"
                                    SelectedValuesChanged="repos => State.AssignRepositoriesAsync(repos)"
                                    Placeholder="Add a repository"
                                    CssClass="inbox-pane__picker"
                                    TestId="inbox-detail-repos" />
                    @if (State.RepositoryOptions.Count == 0)
                    {
                        <Alert BaseClass="inbox-pane__note"
                               Role="status"
                               Message="No repositories are configured in Settings, so the entry will not be targeted at one."
                               TestId="inbox-detail-no-repos" />
                    }

                    @* A particular review date sits with the pickers: a date is a
                       field before it is an act. The decisions bar's Defer offers
                       the quick dates. *@
                    <div class="inbox-pane__defer" data-testid="inbox-detail-defer">
                        <TextField Label="Review on"
                                   Type="date"
                                   Compact="true"
                                   Value="@_deferDate"
                                   ValueChanged="value => _deferDate = value"
                                   CssClass="inbox-pane__defer-date"
                                   TestId="inbox-defer-date" />
                        <ButtonGroup AriaLabel="Deferral" CssClass="inbox-pane__defer-actions" TestId="inbox-defer-actions">
                            <AppButton Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                       Disabled="@Busy"
                                       Title="Back in the inbox on the review date; with no date, it stays aside until you return it"
                                       OnClick="() => State.DeferAsync(ParseDate(_deferDate))"
                                       TestId="inbox-defer">@(item.Status == InboxStatus.Deferred ? "Change date" : "Defer")</AppButton>
                            @if (item.Status == InboxStatus.Deferred)
                            {
                                <AppButton Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                           Disabled="@Busy"
                                           OnClick="State.ResurfaceAsync"
                                           TestId="inbox-return">Return to inbox</AppButton>
                            }
                        </ButtonGroup>
                    </div>
                }
                else if (item.Tags.Count > 0 || item.RepoIds.Count > 0)
                {
                    @* Read-only once decided: the tags and repositories are what the
                       entries were made with, and editing them here would edit nothing. *@
                    <p class="inbox-pane__chips" data-testid="inbox-detail-chips">
                        @foreach (var tag in item.Tags)
                        {
                            <TagChip Text="@TagText.Display(tag.Name)" CssClass="inbox-pane__tag" />
                        }
                        @foreach (var repoId in item.RepoIds)
                        {
                            <Badge Kind="kind" Slug="repository" CssClass="inbox-pane__repository" Title="@($"Repository: {repoId}")">@State.RepositoryAlias(repoId)</Badge>
                        }
                    </p>
                }
            </div>
        </article>

        @* The four decisions, fixed at the foot of the column, each naming its
           key. A decided item keeps only Move to list, which is allowed in
           every state. *@
        <footer class="inbox-pane__decide" role="group" aria-label="Decide" data-testid="inbox-detail-decisions">
            @if (open)
            {
                <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.Primary"
                           Disabled="@(State.PlanRunning || State.BulkRunning)"
                           Busy="@State.RouteRunning"
                           BusyLabel="Moving to backlog"
                           Title="@($"{RouteTitle(repos)} (r)")"
                           OnClick="State.RouteToBacklogAsync"
                           TestId="inbox-move-to-backlog"><span class="inbox-pane__decision-label">@RouteLabel(repos)</span> <kbd class="inbox-pane__key inbox-pane__key--on-primary" aria-hidden="true">R</kbd></AppButton>
            }
            <AppButton Disabled="@Busy"
                       Title="File it in one of your lists (l)"
                       OnClick="() => _moveOpen = true"
                       TestId="inbox-move-to-list"><span class="inbox-pane__decision-label">Move to list</span> <kbd class="inbox-pane__key" aria-hidden="true">L</kbd></AppButton>
            @if (open)
            {
                <AppButton Disabled="@Busy"
                           Title="Put it aside until a review date (d)"
                           OnClick="OpenDefer"
                           TestId="inbox-decide-defer"><span class="inbox-pane__decision-label">Defer</span> <kbd class="inbox-pane__key" aria-hidden="true">D</kbd></AppButton>
                <AppButton Disabled="@Busy"
                           Title="Dismiss it, findable later (a)"
                           OnClick="State.ArchiveAsync"
                           TestId="inbox-archive"><span class="inbox-pane__decision-label">Archive</span> <kbd class="inbox-pane__key" aria-hidden="true">A</kbd></AppButton>
            }
            <span class="inbox-pane__hint inbox-pane__decide-hint"><kbd class="inbox-pane__key">J</kbd> <kbd class="inbox-pane__key">K</kbd> to browse</span>
        </footer>

        <Modal Open="@_moveOpen"
               OpenChanged="open => _moveOpen = open"
               Title="Move to list"
               CssClass="inbox-pane__dialog"
               TestId="inbox-move-list-dialog">
            <ChildContent>
                <MenuList Items="@MoveTargets(item)"
                          AriaLabel="Lists"
                          TestId="inbox-move-list"
                          OnItemSelected="OnMoveTargetAsync" />
            </ChildContent>
        </Modal>

        @* The two relation pickers: a search over a menu, the related ones first
           with their reason beside the title. Filtering is local — the lists are
           already in hand — so the search answers on every keystroke. *@
        <Modal Open="@_duplicateOpen"
               OpenChanged="open => _duplicateOpen = open"
               Title="Archive as duplicate of…"
               CssClass="inbox-pane__dialog"
               TestId="inbox-duplicate-dialog">
            <ChildContent>
                <div class="inbox-pane__picker-dialog" @onkeydown:stopPropagation="true">
                    <SearchBox Value="@_duplicateQuery"
                               ValueChanged="query => _duplicateQuery = query"
                               Placeholder="Find an item"
                               AriaLabel="Find an item"
                               DebounceMilliseconds="0"
                               TestId="inbox-duplicate-search" />
                    @if (DuplicateChoices() is { Count: > 0 } choices)
                    {
                        <MenuList Items="@choices"
                                  AriaLabel="Items"
                                  CssClass="inbox-pane__picker-menu"
                                  TestId="inbox-duplicate-choices"
                                  OnItemSelected="OnDuplicateChosenAsync" />
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <Alert BaseClass="inbox-pane__note"
                               Role="status"
                               Message="No other item matches."
                               TestId="inbox-duplicate-none" />
                    }
                </div>
            </ChildContent>
        </Modal>

        <Modal Open="@_linkOpen"
               OpenChanged="open => _linkOpen = open"
               Title="Link to task…"
               CssClass="inbox-pane__dialog"
               TestId="inbox-link-dialog">
            <ChildContent>
                <div class="inbox-pane__picker-dialog" @onkeydown:stopPropagation="true">
                    <SearchBox Value="@_linkQuery"
                               ValueChanged="query => _linkQuery = query"
                               Placeholder="Find a task"
                               AriaLabel="Find a task"
                               DebounceMilliseconds="0"
                               TestId="inbox-link-search" />
                    @if (LinkChoices() is { Count: > 0 } choices)
                    {
                        <MenuList Items="@choices"
                                  AriaLabel="Tasks"
                                  CssClass="inbox-pane__picker-menu"
                                  TestId="inbox-link-choices"
                                  OnItemSelected="OnLinkChosenAsync" />
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <Alert BaseClass="inbox-pane__note"
                               Role="status"
                               Message="No task matches."
                               TestId="inbox-link-none" />
                    }
                </div>
            </ChildContent>
        </Modal>

        @* Confirmed because nothing is kept: Archive is the undoable dismissal,
           and the message says so rather than leaving the difference to guess. *@
        <ConfirmDialog Open="@_deleteOpen"
                       Title="Delete this item?"
                       Message="@DeleteMessage(item)"
                       ConfirmText="Delete item"
                       Destructive="true"
                       OnConfirm="OnDeleteConfirmedAsync"
                       OnCancel="() => _deleteOpen = false"
                       TestId="inbox-delete-dialog"
                       ConfirmTestId="inbox-delete-confirm"
                       CancelTestId="inbox-delete-cancel" />

        @* The keyboard's way to defer: the review dates a triage decision
           reaches for, one key and Enter away. A particular date is still the
           field beside the pickers — this is the quick half, not a second
           date picker. *@
        <Modal Open="@_deferOpen"
               OpenChanged="open => _deferOpen = open"
               Title="Defer until"
               CssClass="inbox-pane__dialog"
               TestId="inbox-defer-dialog">
            <ChildContent>
                <MenuList Items="@DeferChoices()"
                          AriaLabel="Review dates"
                          TestId="inbox-defer-choices"
                          OnItemSelected="OnDeferChoiceAsync" />
            </ChildContent>
        </Modal>
    }
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public InboxDesktopState State { get; set; } = default!;

    private bool _moveOpen;

    private bool _deleteOpen;

    private static string DeleteMessage(InboxItemDto item) =>
        $"“{Title(item)}” is removed for good. Archive keeps an item findable; delete does not."
        + (item.Routing is null ? "" : " The backlog entries it became stay where they are.");

    private async Task OnDeleteConfirmedAsync()
    {
        _deleteOpen = false;
        await State.DeleteAsync();
    }

    /// <summary>The review date as the date field holds it, <c>yyyy-MM-dd</c> or
    /// empty. Held here until "Defer" is pressed rather than written on every
    /// change, because a date field reports half-typed dates as empty.</summary>
    private string? _deferDate;

    /// <summary>The item <see cref="_deferDate"/> was filled for, so choosing
    /// another item — or the same one coming back with a new date — refills it.</summary>
    private (Guid Id, DateOnly? Until)? _deferFilledFor;

    protected override void OnParametersSet()
    {
        if (State.SelectedItem is not { } item) return;

        var current = (item.Id, item.DeferredUntil);
        if (_deferFilledFor == current) return;

        _deferFilledFor = current;
        _deferDate = item.DeferredUntil?.ToString("yyyy-MM-dd", System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture);
    }

    private static DateOnly? ParseDate(string? value) =>
        DateOnly.TryParseExact(value, "yyyy-MM-dd", System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture,
            System.Globalization.DateTimeStyles.None, out var date)
            ? date
            : null;

    private bool Busy => State.RoutingInFlight;

    // --- Suggestions --------------------------------------------------------

    /// <summary>The digit keys that take a suggestion. Only a bare digit: with a
    /// modifier held the key is somebody else's shortcut.</summary>
    private Task OnShortcutKeyAsync(KeyboardEventArgs e) =>
        e.CtrlKey || e.AltKey || e.MetaKey || e.ShiftKey ? Task.CompletedTask : State.AcceptShortcutAsync(e.Key);

    // The chip's words are triage's too: InboxSuggestionWords holds them once.
    private string SuggestionText(InboxSuggestionDto suggestion) => InboxSuggestionWords.Text(State, suggestion);

    private string SuggestionLabel(InboxSuggestionDto suggestion) => InboxSuggestionWords.Label(State, suggestion);

    private static string SuggestionTestId(InboxSuggestionDto suggestion) => InboxSuggestionWords.TestId(suggestion);

    private (bool Available, string? Reason) Availability => State.PlanDrafterAvailability;

    private static string Title(InboxItemDto item) =>
        string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(item.Title) ? "Untitled" : item.Title;

    /// <summary>"Video · YouTube": the kind and the channel, which are two facts
    /// — a video arrives from the monitor, from the phone, or by hand.</summary>
    private static string Eyebrow(InboxItemDto item) =>
        $"{InboxLabels.Kind(item.KindSlug)} · {InboxLabels.Channel(item.Channel)}";

    private static IReadOnlyList<string> TagNames(InboxItemDto item) =>
        [.. item.Tags.Select(tag => tag.Name)];

    /// <summary>The label says how many entries the act makes when repositories
    /// are chosen: one per repository. With none chosen it makes one untargeted
    /// entry, and the label does not need to say so.</summary>
    private static string RouteLabel(int repos) =>
        repos == 0 ? "Move to backlog" : $"Move to backlog → {InboxDesktopState.Counted(repos, "task", "tasks")}";

    private static string RouteTitle(int repos) => repos switch
    {
        0 => "Create one backlog entry from this item",
        1 => "Create one backlog entry targeted at the chosen repository",
        _ => $"Create {repos} backlog entries, one per chosen repository"
    };

    private string StateLine(InboxItemDto item) => item switch
    {
        { Status: InboxStatus.Archived, DuplicateOf: not null, DuplicateOfTask: true } =>
            "Merged into a backlog task and archived.",
        { Status: InboxStatus.Archived, DuplicateOf: { } original } =>
            State.Items.FirstOrDefault(other => other.Id == original) is { } kept
                ? $"Archived as a duplicate of “{Title(kept)}”."
                : "Archived as a duplicate of an item that is no longer in the Inbox.",
        { Status: InboxStatus.Archived } => "Archived.",
        { Status: InboxStatus.Deferred, DeferredUntil: { } until } =>
            $"Deferred until {until.ToString("d MMM yyyy", System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)}.",
        { Status: InboxStatus.Deferred } => "Deferred with no review date.",
        { Routing: { } routing } =>
            $"Routed to {InboxDesktopState.Counted(routing.TaskIds.Count, "task", "tasks")} on {routing.RoutedAt.ToLocalTime().ToString("d MMM yyyy", System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)}.",
        _ => InboxLabels.Status(item.Status) + "."
    };

    // --- Kind blocks -------------------------------------------------------

    // Razor templates rather than hand-written builder calls, so the sequence
    // numbers are the compiler's: several of these render one after another
    // inside one block, and hand-numbered fragments that each start at zero
    // give the differ a sequence that runs backwards between them.

    /// <summary>The body as markdown, or the kind's own line for an item that
    /// arrived with only a title — the ordinary case for a synced capture, so it
    /// reads as a fact rather than a fault. Null says the kind has nothing to
    /// say about an empty body.</summary>
    private static RenderFragment Prose(InboxItemDto item, string? emptyLine) => @<text>
        @if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(item.BodyMd))
        {
            @if (emptyLine is not null)
            {
                @Note(emptyLine)
            }
        }
        else
        {
            <div class="inbox-pane__prose" data-testid="inbox-detail-body">
                <MarkdownView Blocks="@MarkdownPreview.ParseDocument(item.BodyMd)" />
            </div>
        }
    </text>;

    // --- Attachments -------------------------------------------------------

    // Instance templates rather than static ones, because both read the state:
    // which thumbnails have been read, and which row a Retry is running for.

    /// <summary>The pictures the capture arrived with, above the body. Each one
    /// is a button that opens the file, so the picture is the way to the full
    /// size rather than a dead image. A picture not read yet leaves its tile out
    /// rather than drawing a broken one; the next render brings it.</summary>
    private RenderFragment Thumbnails(InboxItemDto item) => @<text>
        @{ var pictures = item.Attachments.Where(InboxDesktopState.ShowsAsThumbnail).ToList(); }
        @if (pictures.Count > 0)
        {
            <ul class="inbox-pane__thumbnails" aria-label="Pictures" data-testid="inbox-detail-thumbnails">
                @foreach (var picture in pictures)
                {
                    <li class="inbox-pane__thumbnail-item" data-testid="inbox-detail-thumbnail-item">
                        <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.None"
                                   BaseClass="inbox-pane__thumbnail-button"
                                   Title="@($"Open {picture.Name}")"
                                   OnClick="() => State.OpenAttachmentAsync(picture.Id)"
                                   TestId="@($"inbox-attachment-thumbnail-{picture.Id:N}")">
                            @if (State.Thumbnail(picture.Id) is { } source)
                            {
                                <img class="inbox-pane__attachment-image" src="@source" alt="@picture.Name" data-testid="inbox-detail-attachment-image" />
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                <span class="inbox-pane__thumbnail-pending">@picture.Name</span>
                            }
                        </AppButton>
                    </li>
                }
            </ul>
        }
    </text>;

    /// <summary>One row per file that is not drawn as a thumbnail: its name and
    /// size, Open when it is on this machine, and Retry with the reason when its
    /// download failed. A file still waiting for its first fetch says so.</summary>
    private RenderFragment FileRows(InboxItemDto item) => @<text>
        @{ var files = item.Attachments.Where(attachment => !InboxDesktopState.ShowsAsThumbnail(attachment)).ToList(); }
        @if (files.Count > 0)
        {
            <ul class="inbox-pane__files" aria-label="Files" data-testid="inbox-detail-files">
                @foreach (var file in files)
                {
                    <li class="inbox-pane__file" data-testid="@($"inbox-attachment-row-{file.Id:N}")">
                        <span class="inbox-pane__file-name">@file.Name</span>
                        <span class="inbox-pane__file-size">@Size(file.SizeBytes)</span>
                        @if (file.Downloaded)
                        {
                            <AppButton Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                       OnClick="() => State.OpenAttachmentAsync(file.Id)"
                                       TestId="@($"inbox-attachment-open-{file.Id:N}")">Open</AppButton>
                        }
                        else if (file.LastError is { } error)
                        {
                            <AppButton Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                       Busy="@(State.RetryingAttachmentId == file.Id)"
                                       BusyLabel="Downloading"
                                       Disabled="@(State.RetryingAttachmentId is not null)"
                                       OnClick="() => State.RetryAttachmentAsync(file.Id)"
                                       TestId="@($"inbox-attachment-retry-{file.Id:N}")">Retry</AppButton>
                            <Alert BaseClass="inbox-pane__file-error"
                                   Role="status"
                                   Message="@error"
                                   TestId="@($"inbox-attachment-error-{file.Id:N}")" />
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <Alert BaseClass="inbox-pane__file-state"
                                   Role="status"
                                   Message="Waiting to download"
                                   TestId="@($"inbox-attachment-waiting-{file.Id:N}")" />
                        }
                    </li>
                }
            </ul>
        }
    </text>;

    /// <summary>A size the way a file manager writes one.</summary>
    internal static string Size(long bytes) => bytes switch
    {
        < 1024 => $"{bytes} B",
        < 1024 * 1024 => (bytes / 1024d).ToString("0.#", System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture) + " KB",
        _ => (bytes / (1024d * 1024)).ToString("0.#", System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture) + " MB",
    };

    /// <summary>Reads the thumbnails and the suggestions of the item on screen. A
    /// parameter set is every render the pane asks for — the state is the one
    /// parameter, and it is an object, so Blazor always hands it on — and both
    /// reads are no-ops once the item's are in hand.</summary>
    protected override async Task OnParametersSetAsync()
    {
        if (State.SelectedItem is { Attachments.Count: > 0 } item) await State.LoadThumbnailsAsync(item);

        await State.LoadSuggestionsAsync();
        await State.LoadRelationsAsync();
    }

    private static RenderFragment Note(string line) =>
        @<Alert BaseClass="inbox-pane__note" Role="status" Message="@line" TestId="inbox-detail-no-body" />;

    private static RenderFragment Link(string? url) => @<text>
        @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(url))
        {
            <a class="inbox-pane__link" href="@url" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-testid="inbox-detail-link">@url</a>
        }
    </text>;

    private static RenderFragment Attachment(string? url) => @<text>
        @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(url))
        {
            <a class="inbox-pane__link inbox-pane__link--attachment" href="@url" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-testid="inbox-detail-attachment">@AttachmentName(url)</a>
        }
    </text>;

    /// <summary>The file name at the end of the URL, which is what a reader
    /// recognises an attachment by; the whole URL when there is no path to cut.</summary>
    private static string AttachmentName(string url)
    {
        if (Uri.TryCreate(url, UriKind.Absolute, out var uri))
        {
            var name = Uri.UnescapeDataString(uri.Segments[^1].Trim('/'));
            if (name.Length > 0) return name;
        }

        return url;
    }

    /// <summary>The video id, from either spelling of a YouTube URL, or null
    /// when the URL is not one — a video captured from elsewhere gets a link
    /// and no thumbnail rather than a broken image.</summary>
    internal static string? YouTubeVideoId(string? url)
    {
        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(url) || !Uri.TryCreate(url, UriKind.Absolute, out var uri)) return null;

        var host = uri.Host.ToLowerInvariant();

        if (host is "youtu.be" or "www.youtu.be")
        {
            return Clean(uri.AbsolutePath.Trim('/'));
        }

        if (host is "youtube.com" or "www.youtube.com" or "m.youtube.com")
        {
            if (uri.AbsolutePath.StartsWith("/watch", StringComparison.Ordinal))
            {
                var query = System.Web.HttpUtility.ParseQueryString(uri.Query);
                return Clean(query["v"]);
            }

            var segments = uri.AbsolutePath.Trim('/').Split('/');
            if (segments.Length >= 2 && segments[0] is "shorts" or "embed" or "live")
            {
                return Clean(segments[1]);
            }
        }

        return null;

        static string? Clean(string? id) =>
            string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(id) || id.Any(c => !(char.IsLetterOrDigit(c) || c is '-' or '_')) ? null : id;
    }

    /// <summary>The language a fenced block names, so the code view highlights
    /// it; null for a bare fence or none, which the view reads as plain.</summary>
    private static string? CodeLanguage(string body)
    {
        var firstLine = body.TrimStart().Split('\n')[0].Trim();
        if (!firstLine.StartsWith("```", StringComparison.Ordinal)) return null;

        var language = firstLine[3..].Trim();
        return language.Length == 0 ? null : language;
    }

    // --- Relations ----------------------------------------------------------

    private bool _duplicateOpen;

    private string? _duplicateQuery;

    private bool _linkOpen;

    private string? _linkQuery;

    private static string TitleOf(string title) => string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(title) ? "Untitled" : title;

    /// <summary>Opens "Archive as duplicate of…" on an empty search.</summary>
    private void OpenDuplicatePicker()
    {
        if (!CanDecide) return;

        _duplicateQuery = null;
        _duplicateOpen = true;
    }

    /// <summary>Opens "Link to task…" on an empty search.</summary>
    private void OpenLinkPicker()
    {
        if (!CanDecide) return;

        _linkQuery = null;
        _linkOpen = true;
    }

    /// <summary>The items the duplicate picker offers, a related one with its
    /// reason after the title.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<MenuItem> DuplicateChoices() =>
        [.. State.DuplicateCandidates(_duplicateQuery).Select(other =>
            new MenuItem(other.Id.ToString("N"), State.RelationReason(other.Id) is { } reason ? $"{TitleOf(other.Title)} · {reason}" : TitleOf(other.Title)))];

    /// <summary>The tasks the link picker offers, a related one with its reason
    /// and a finished one saying so.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<MenuItem> LinkChoices() =>
        [.. State.LinkCandidates(_linkQuery).Select(task =>
            new MenuItem(task.Id.ToString("N"), string.Join(" · ", new[] { TitleOf(task.Title), task.Reason, task.IsOpen ? null : "Done" }.OfType<string>())))];

    private async Task OnDuplicateChosenAsync(MenuItem choice)
    {
        _duplicateOpen = false;
        if (Guid.TryParseExact(choice.Id, "N", out var original)) await State.ArchiveAsDuplicateAsync(original);
    }

    private async Task OnLinkChosenAsync(MenuItem choice)
    {
        _linkOpen = false;
        if (Guid.TryParseExact(choice.Id, "N", out var taskId)) await State.LinkToTaskAsync(taskId);
    }

    // --- Move to list ------------------------------------------------------

    /// <summary>Every list but the one the item is in, with its group's name
    /// in front so two lists called "Reading" in two groups can be told apart,
    /// and the inbox itself when the item is filed somewhere.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<MenuItem> MoveTargets(InboxItemDto item) => InboxDecisionMenus.MoveTargets(State, item);

    // --- Opened from the keyboard -------------------------------------------

    /// <summary>The tag field's input, which the pane focuses for <c>g</c>.</summary>
    public const string TagsInputId = "inbox-detail-tags-input";

    /// <summary>Whether the item on screen can still be decided on — the acts
    /// a shortcut reaches are the ones the decisions bar offers.</summary>
    public bool CanDecide => State.SelectedItem is { Status: InboxStatus.Unprocessed or InboxStatus.Deferred } && !Busy;

    /// <summary>Opens "Move to list", as <c>l</c> does. Filing is allowed in
    /// every state, so only a missing item or a run in flight refuses it.</summary>
    public void OpenMove()
    {
        if (State.SelectedItem is null || Busy) return;

        _moveOpen = true;
        _ = InvokeAsync(StateHasChanged);
    }

    /// <summary>Opens the review dates, as <c>d</c> does.</summary>
    public void OpenDefer()
    {
        if (!CanDecide) return;

        _deferOpen = true;
        _ = InvokeAsync(StateHasChanged);
    }

    private bool _deferOpen;

    private IReadOnlyList<MenuItem> DeferChoices() => InboxDecisionMenus.DeferChoices(State.Today);

    private async Task OnDeferChoiceAsync(MenuItem choice)
    {
        _deferOpen = false;
        await InboxDecisionMenus.DeferAsync(State, choice);
    }

    private async Task OnMoveTargetAsync(MenuItem target)
    {
        _moveOpen = false;
        await InboxDecisionMenus.MoveAsync(State, target);
    }
}
